1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,660
Moving on to endocarditis,

2
00:00:01,660 --> 00:00:04,500
this is inflammation of the endocardium,

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,640
particularly the endocardium that lines

4
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,540
the surface of cardiac valves.

5
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:11,580
Now recall that the heart basically contains three layers.

6
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:14,580
There's an endocardium, there's a myocardium,

7
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:16,820
and then there is a epicardium.

8
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:18,620
Remember that the endocardium lines

9
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,180
the inner surface of the heart.

10
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:21,780
It's basically a single layer of cells

11
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:23,700
sitting on top of a basement membrane.

12
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,560
They're basically endothelial cells.

13
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,400
And that this endocardium also lines

14
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,000
the surface of the cardiac valves as they project out.

15
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,940
And so in endocarditis, you're gonna get inflammation

16
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:35,980
predominantly on the surface of those cardiac valves.

17
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:38,580
Now this is usually due to bacterial infection,

18
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,080
not always, but usually.

19
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:43,680
The first high yield bug to be aware of is strep viridans.

20
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:46,980
This is the most common overall cause of endocarditis,

21
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:49,720
and it is a low virulence organism.

22
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:52,320
Now that's important because number one,

23
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:56,160
therefore, it can only infect previously damaged valves.

24
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:58,060
For example, if the valve is damaged

25
00:00:58,060 --> 00:00:59,660
by chronic rheumatic heart disease

26
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,900
or mitral valve prolapse, then and only then

27
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:05,440
will this low virulence organism be able to infect it.

28
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,360
And number two, because it's low virulence,

29
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:09,300
it results in small vegetations

30
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:11,440
that will not destroy the valve.

31
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:13,080
And so that's particularly high yield,

32
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:16,280
but all of that's based on the low virulence of the organism.

33
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:19,080
In fact, the endocarditis caused by strep viridans

34
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:21,080
is also called subacute.

35
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:23,020
Now the pathogenesis is that because you've got

36
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:24,820
a previously damaged valve,

37
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:28,820
that damaged endocardial surface will expose subendothelial

38
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:32,360
collagen and tissue factor underneath it.

39
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:34,360
That then allows for the development of thrombotic

40
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:36,940
vegetations, and those vegetations, of course,

41
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:39,160
contain both platelets and fibrin.

42
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:44,600
Now these vegetations, they act as a trap for bacteria

43
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:48,040
whenever there's transient bacteria in the blood.

44
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:50,520
So for example, let's say that there's a dental procedure

45
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:52,680
and that forces bacteria into the blood.

46
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,900
Some of those bacteria can then be trapped

47
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:58,120
in these thrombotic vegetations on the heart valves,

48
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:01,360
which will then result in infectious endocarditis.

49
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,800
And that's one reason, for example,

50
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:06,340
the classic teaching was that prophylaxis with antibiotics,

51
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:09,140
for example, during the time of dental procedure,

52
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:11,840
could theoretically decrease the risk of endocarditis

53
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,880
in patients with damaged valves.

54
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:16,680
Staph aureus is the most common cause of endocarditis

55
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:18,420
in IV drug abusers.

56
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:20,280
It is a high virulence organism.

57
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,880
Therefore, it will infect normal valves,

58
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,680
and it will result in large vegetations

59
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:27,120
that destroy the valve.

60
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:30,320
Hence, it causes something called acute endocarditis.

61
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:32,160
Now important to know that the classic valve

62
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:33,920
that's going to be involved by Staph aureus

63
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:35,260
is the tricuspid.

64
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:37,400
Again, the idea is that the IV drug abuser

65
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,760
has contaminated skin and then shoots up

66
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,360
through the contaminated skin.

67
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:44,440
When they do so, the Staph aureus gets into the vein,

68
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:46,540
gets drained into the right heart eventually,

69
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:48,140
and then hits the tricuspid valve

70
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,380
and will damage the tricuspid valve.

71
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:53,180
Here's a picture of Staph aureus endocarditis.

72
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:55,580
You'll notice that these are very large vegetations

73
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:57,180
sitting on the cardiac valve,

74
00:02:57,180 --> 00:03:00,980
and of course, this is also called acute endocarditis.

75
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:04,320
Staph epidermidis is important because it is the key bug

76
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:07,300
that causes endocarditis of prosthetic valves,

77
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:08,920
so that's the high yield there,

78
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,800
and Strep bulvis is important because it is the key bug

79
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:13,600
that causes endocarditis in patients

80
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:16,160
with underlying colorectal carcinoma.

81
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:19,380
Now, this is very high yield for board exam purposes,

82
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:21,000
even for clinics for that matter.

83
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,080
If you have a patient with endocarditis

84
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:25,940
who ends up having endocarditis due to Strep bulvis,

85
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:27,140
the next thing you need to do

86
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:29,640
is check for colorectal carcinoma,

87
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:32,080
and so that's a particularly important association

88
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,860
for board examinations.

89
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:35,820
Now, it's also possible to get endocarditis

90
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:39,700
with a group of organisms called the Haysack organisms.

91
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,100
This word basically represents the key organisms

92
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:44,200
that can cause this type of endocarditis.

93
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:47,400
They include Haemophilus, Actinobacillus,

94
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:50,740
Cardiobacterium, Iconella, and Kingella,

95
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:52,540
and the key thing about this endocarditis

96
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:53,920
is that it gives you endocarditis

97
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:55,740
with negative blood cultures,

98
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:57,480
and that's of course because these organisms

99
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:59,860
are particularly difficult to grow,

100
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:02,780
and so again, endocarditis with negative blood cultures.

101
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:05,560
Think about the Haysack organisms.

102
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:07,920
Clinically, irrespective of the cause of endocarditis,

103
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:09,660
patients generally have fever,

104
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:11,100
and they also have a murmur.

105
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:12,200
Now, the reason they have a murmur

106
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:13,800
is because they've got these vegetations

107
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,900
on the cardiac valves,

108
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:18,200
which is then going to disrupt flow across those valves.

109
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:20,940
In addition, they can get septic embolization

110
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:22,780
of the vegetations on the valve.

111
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:24,940
Now again, the idea is that if this is the valve

112
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:26,440
coming off the wall of the heart,

113
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:29,260
you've got these vegetations sitting on top of the valve,

114
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:31,120
and of course, the vegetations are going to be

115
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:33,080
flapping up and down with the valve,

116
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:36,500
and so these vegetations can be shot off into the circulation,

117
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,560
and when they're shot off into the circulation,

118
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:41,660
that would eventually result in septic emboli

119
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:44,260
of these tiny pieces of bacteria.

120
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:46,760
Complications of septic embolizations include

121
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,060
Janeway lesions,

122
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:50,440
and these are erythematous, non-tender lesions

123
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,080
on the palms and the soles,

124
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:54,880
and Osler nodes, which are painful lesions

125
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:56,580
on the fingers or toes,

126
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,740
and the way to remember this is,

127
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,680
ouch, ouch, Osler,

128
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:02,260
and so that's the one that's painful, if that helps you.

129
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:05,060
In addition, you can get splinter hemorrhages in the nail bed,

130
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:07,560
and that again would be due to septic embolization,

131
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:09,600
and so these are some of the key findings

132
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:12,200
that arise with septic embolization.

133
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,840
Now finally, the patients can also have

134
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:15,340
anemia of chronic disease.

135
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:17,180
Of course, they've got chronic inflammation

136
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:19,520
because they've got this infectious endocarditis,

137
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:22,420
which can then lead to anemia of chronic disease.

138
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:24,280
Now the laboratory findings are that the patient

139
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:26,820
will generally have a positive blood culture.

140
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:29,360
There will be the findings of anemia of chronic disease,

141
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:32,020
and just recall that if they have anemia of chronic disease,

142
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:35,960
that's going to be generally a microcytic anemia,

143
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,420
and so the hemoglobin would be low because there's anemia.

144
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:41,560
The MCV would be low because it's usually microcytic.

145
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:44,100
Of course, in this particular case,

146
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:47,200
you've got acute phase reactants being released by the liver.

147
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:50,580
One particular acute phase reactants would be hepcidin.

148
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:52,280
Remember, hepcidin is high yield.

149
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:54,780
It traps iron in the storage sites,

150
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:56,620
and so when iron is trapped in the storage sites,

151
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:57,880
the ferritin will be high.

152
00:05:57,880 --> 00:06:00,740
Because the ferritin is high, the TiVC will be low,

153
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:03,340
and in addition, because there's no access to iron

154
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:04,680
from the storage sites,

155
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:07,140
the bone marrow will begin to take iron from the blood,

156
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:08,980
and so the serum iron will decrease,

157
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:11,180
and the percent saturation will decrease.

158
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:14,080
Now in addition, transesophageal echo can be used

159
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:16,080
for detecting lesions on the valves,

160
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,600
and this is a very good way to be able to look for those

161
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:21,200
vegetations on the valve that are so characteristic

162
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,700
of endocarditis.

163
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:25,240
Another type of endocarditis is called

164
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,700
non-bacterial thrombotic endocarditis.

165
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:30,740
The name tells you a lot, it's not due to bacteria.

166
00:06:30,740 --> 00:06:33,040
Instead, you get thrombotic vegetations

167
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,900
on the cardiac valves.

168
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:36,540
These are sterile vegetations.

169
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:39,740
They generally are associated with a hypercoagulable state

170
00:06:39,740 --> 00:06:42,940
or an underlying adenocarcinoma in the patient.

171
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:45,920
These vegetations usually arise on the mitral valve,

172
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:47,820
along the lines of closure,

173
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:50,160
and they'll result in regurgitation.

174
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,700
Liebman-Sachs endocarditis is particularly high yield.

175
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:54,300
We've discussed it previously.

176
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:56,060
This is where you get sterile vegetations

177
00:06:56,060 --> 00:06:57,840
in association with lupus.

178
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:59,400
Now the most important thing here is that

179
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:00,740
if you've got this valve,

180
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:05,040
you get vegetations on both sides of the cardiac valve.

181
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:06,940
And when you get vegetations on both sides,

182
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:10,780
that's highly characteristic of Liebman-Sachs endocarditis.

183
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:12,880
Again, it usually involves the mitral valve,

184
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:16,180
and it's gonna result in mitral valve regurgitation.

185
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:18,820
And that completes our section on endocarditis.

